WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.000
“Who's paid. What's next.” A tenant phone scrolls toward Unit 101. The large balance reads ₱81,675, matching the app's Unit 101 card as it comes into view. Demo data.

00:00:03.000 --> 00:00:04.900
“Report the payment.” The tenant taps Pay this rental (green rings mark real taps), and the real payment form opens. Demo data.

00:00:04.900 --> 00:00:08.000
The tenant selects a method, enters ₱16,500 and a reference, then attaches a synthetic receipt. Demo data. Sped up 2x.

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:09.500
The tenant taps Submit. The app confirms the report. Demo data.

00:00:09.500 --> 00:00:10.500
“Submitted. Awaiting review.” Back home, Unit 101 still shows ₱81,675, unchanged until checked. Demo data.

00:00:10.500 --> 00:00:12.000
“The landlord checks it.” A second phone slides in; the tenant's pending screen holds while the landlord opens the payment review. Demo data. Landlord footage sped up 2x.

00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:16.000
The landlord reviews the ₱16,500 report and matching charges, then taps Approve. The app says “Payment recorded” and “Receipt #152 issued.” The tenant phone still shows the pending ₱81,675 balance. Demo data.

00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:20.000
“Checked. Recorded.” The tenant phone changes to its approved home view. Unit 101 and the large balance both read ₱65,175. A soft bell sounds as the approved state appears; the balance holds. Demo data.

00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:24.000
Tenant101 · tommydeleon.com. Team project · Not launched · Demo data. A closing card shows the approved tenant screen.
